WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.218
Hi! 4 plates with 3 apples on each. How many apples altogether? Today we'll learn multiplication.

2
00:00:10.368 --> 00:00:14.130
We multiply when every group has the same amount.

3
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.394
4 plates of 3 is 4 threes.

4
00:00:17.544 --> 00:00:22.386
We can add: 3 plus 3 plus 3 plus 3 is 12.

5
00:00:22.536 --> 00:00:28.170
Multiplication is quicker: 4 times 3 is 12.

6
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.474
Count in twos: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10.

7
00:00:33.624 --> 00:00:38.586
Count in fives: 5, 10, 15, 20.

8
00:00:38.736 --> 00:00:42.882
5 twos: count in twos 5 times, that's 10.

9
00:00:43.032 --> 00:00:47.778
Count in tens: 4 tens is 40.

10
00:00:47.928 --> 00:00:52.146
Watch out! 4 threes is not 4 plus 3!

11
00:00:52.296 --> 00:00:56.442
4 threes is 3 plus 3 plus 3 plus 3.

12
00:00:56.592 --> 00:01:01.098
Write it as 4 times 3, which is 12.

13
00:01:01.248 --> 00:01:08.922
Your turn! What are 3 fives? Pause and think.

14
00:01:09.072 --> 00:01:15.930
5, 10, 15. It's 15. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:27.138
Another one! How do we write 2 plus 2 plus 2 plus 2 plus 2 plus 2 with times? Pause and think.

16
00:01:27.288 --> 00:01:33.810
There are 6 twos: 6 times 2 is 12. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:41.946
Here's another! What is 4 times 5? Pause and think.

18
00:01:42.096 --> 00:01:49.602
5, 10, 15, 20. It's 20. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:49.752 --> 00:01:57.738
Try one more! What is 3 times 10? Pause and think.

20
00:01:57.888 --> 00:02:04.146
10, 20, 30. It's 30. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:04.296 --> 00:02:14.634
Try one more! 5 bags with 4 oranges in each. How many oranges? Pause and think.

22
00:02:14.784 --> 00:02:21.114
5 fours: 5 times 4 is 20. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:21.264 --> 00:02:31.266
Try one more! 7 pairs of socks. How many socks altogether? Pause and think.

24
00:02:31.416 --> 00:02:38.010
A pair is 2, so 7 times 2 is 14. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:45.906
Last one! What is 8 times 4? Pause and think.

26
00:02:46.056 --> 00:02:54.042
4 fours is 16; 8 fours is two 16s, 32. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:54.192 --> 00:03:00.570
Remember: equal groups can be written with times. Skip counting helps you work it out.

28
00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.465
Find things in pairs at home and multiply!

